    title: "BSI更新《技術指引 TR-03183》：提供企業應對《網路韌性法案》（CRA）的風險基礎指南",
    summary: "德國聯邦資訊安全局（BSI）於 2025 年 10 月初更新了《技術指引 BSI TR-03183》第一部分「一般要求」，並在 it-sa 展會上展示。新版 0.10.0 旨在根據《網路韌性法案》（CRA）的相關要求，為製造商和產品制定安全要求。該指引提供了一種基於風險的 IT 安全措施選擇方法，並包含了一套通用安全措施，以機器可讀格式 OSCAL 發布。此外，BSI 也更新了關於「軟體物料清單」（SBOM）和「漏洞報告與通知」的相關指引。雖然 BSI TR-03183 尚未具備強制性或約束性，但它作為進入 CRA 的入門輔助工具，特別適用於尚未建立成熟開發和漏洞處理流程的製造商。鑑於 CRA 已於 2024 年 12 月生效，企業應利用此指引提前準備，並可透過展示 IT 安全標誌來區隔市場。建議製造商關注指引內容，並可透過官方電子郵件聯繫 BSI 參與進一步的研討會。",
    tags: ["BSI", "Cyber Resilience Act", "CRA", "TR-03183", "SBOM", "OSCAL", "IT安全"],
    title_en: "BSI Updates Technical Guideline TR-03183: Providing a Risk-Based Guide for Enterprises Addressing the Cyber Resilience Act (CRA)",
    summary_en: "The German Federal Office for Information Security (BSI) updated the first part, 'General Requirements,' of the Technical Guideline BSI TR-03183 in early October 2025, and showcased it at the it-sa exhibition. The new version 0.10.0 aims to establish security requirements for manufacturers and products in line with the relevant requirements of the Cyber Resilience Act (CRA). The guideline offers a risk-based method for selecting IT security measures and includes a set of general security measures published in machine-readable format using OSCAL. Furthermore, BSI also updated related guidelines concerning 'Software Bill of Materials' (SBOM) and 'Vulnerability Reporting and Notification.' Although BSI TR-03183 is not yet mandatory or binding, it serves as an introductory aid for entering the CRA, particularly useful for manufacturers that have not yet established mature development and vulnerability handling processes. Given that the CRA took effect in December 2024, enterprises should use this guideline for early preparation and can differentiate themselves in the market by displaying an IT security label. Manufacturers are advised to pay attention to the guideline's content and can contact BSI via official email to participate in further workshops.",
